1. Introduction
The ProgramInterface module provides a command-line interface (CLI) for interacting with the GW-BASIC-like interpreter. It enables the user to input, edit, and submit commands in real-time, with support for special key handling and screen rendering. The module mimics the behavior of a traditional DOS-based GW-BASIC environment with live editing and function key shortcuts.

 implements a console-based command-line editor in C++ with enhanced input handling,
including:
- Arrow key navigation
- Special key commands (F1-F10)
- Cursor-aware input editing
- A REPL that supports interactive editing.
The system mimics retro-style BASIC terminal interfaces and is suitable for embedding into interpreters or
command shells.
  
2. Design Description
The ProgramInterface is designed with modular separation of concerns:

CommandLineEditor: Manages user input, cursor movement, editing, and line submission.

ScreenRenderer: Responsible for drawing the input line and moving the cursor on screen.

SpecialKeyHandler: Intercepts and processes special function keys (F1–F10) by injecting predefined commands into the editor.

These components communicate through shared structures and are integrated with the platform-independent SystemInterface for terminal I/O.

